nodecode-nyx is a rewrite of sixgodgit's sixgodgit/nyx:

  https://github.com/sixgodgit/nyx
  commit 101a64d308281f75ba200e28c1c73c4d6e1887ce
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 NexSandglass
  Copyright (c) 2026 sixgodgit (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is hermes-plugin of that commit, the entry point to the
nyx-memory package: its four promises are kept -- a journal written verbatim
with no model on the write path, secrets replaced before anything is stored,
source and date on every entry, and a forgetting that is two stages deep. Its
journal line (`STAMP | SOURCE | TEXT`) and the labels its secret filter
writes are the original's, so a folder its command line already writes can be
read here. Its tool set is carried over as nyx_remember, nyx_recall,
nyx_forget and nyx_restore, and the section's data_dir, recall budget,
quarantine window and secret switch are the original's settings under the
names a Nodecode section wears. One detail is not carried: the original
keeps a secret's last four characters in its placeholder as a hint, and this
cell writes the label alone.

What was left out, and why: semantic retrieval, which the original reaches
through an embedding model or an external embedding API -- a cell here does
no model call on either path, so recall is by the words of the query; the
bi-temporal fact store, the knowledge graph and the L3 profile built on top
of the journal, which need the Python package's own pipeline; the optional
encrypted vault and its companion reveal plugin, whose keystore and approval
seam are the host's, not a tool cell's; and the MCP server, the
`hermes memory setup` commands and the Chinese localisation, whose answers
the section, /settings and /nyx give. LICENSE is that repository's LICENSE,
unchanged.
